  },
  "scope": {
    "status": "grounded",
    "text": "k-fold cross-validation can be used for model evaluation and model selection, including the selection of the best hyper-parameter value and the final classification model by making effective use of every data instance in the training set. Pre-processing operations, such as feature selection or hyper-parameter tuning, should be performed within the training fold of every run rather than using the entire data set to avoid selection bias.",
